"Husk needs memory it can write and then execute, which on iOS takes an attached debugger. There are two ways to get it: a debugger that services trap requests, or a MAP_JIT mapping, which the kernel allows any debugged process. Either one is enough — which is available depends on the device and the iOS version, so Husk tests both rather than assuming." = "Husk 需要可先写入再执行的内存。在 iOS 上需连接调试器，或使用允许已调试进程执行代码的 MAP_JIT 映射。设备与 iOS 版本支持情况不同，因此 Husk 会实际检测这两种方式。";
"Husk pretends to be a computer on your Wi-Fi, and your %@ pairs with it the way it would with a Mac." = "Husk 在 Wi-Fi 网络中作为电脑出现，你的 %@ 可以像连接 Mac 一样与其配对。";
"Husk restores a saved machine instead of booting it, which takes seconds rather than minutes. The picture freezes while it writes. With this off, nothing saves by itself — including after an install." = "Husk 通过恢复虚拟机存档跳过启动过程，只需几秒而非几分钟。保存期间画面会暂停。关闭后不会自动保存，安装应用后也不会。";
"Husk runs a real Android system and opens APKs inside it. A few questions first — all of them can be changed later in Settings." = "Husk 运行真实的 Android 系统，并在其中打开 APK。先完成几项设置，你可以稍后在“设置”中随时更改。";
"Husk runs unmodified Android APKs in a real Android system on your iPhone. The console shows Husk's live log, the guest's serial output and QEMU's own output — the three files any problem here is diagnosed from." = "Husk 在 iPhone 上的真实 Android 系统中运行未经修改的 APK。控制台显示 Husk 实时日志、Android 串口输出及 QEMU 输出，供排查问题使用。";
"Husk tells you when a new version is out. Install the new IPA over the old one with the same sideloader. Your library, apps and saves are kept." = "Husk 会提示新版本。请通过同一侧载工具覆盖安装新版 IPA，并保持相同签名身份及应用标识，以保留游戏库、应用和存档。不要先卸载旧版。";
